  "body": "Follow-up to #13. The growth-ring planner (`adaptive/grow.rs`) re-walks the whole cleared outline every revolution, so its work grows with the square of the channel length; a 270 mm × 14 mm band would take minutes. #13 bounds it (adaptive/budget.rs: an up-front estimate past 2,000 tool radii and a summed-revolution budget of 30,000 tool radii) and falls back to Offset rings by name. Making the walk incremental (only the changed stretch of the outline per revolution) would let long channels, bands and large islanded pockets keep an adaptive spiral. Also: `adaptive/mod.rs` is at 427 lines - split it on the way (400-line rule).",
